citations.quote:
Let $f\in L^1(\mu)$ and let $\varepsilon>0$. Then there is $\delta>0$ such that
for every measurable $E$,
$$\mu(E)<\delta\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad\int_E|f|\,d\mu<\varepsilon.$$

